# the nudge: a layer's button held (ENV the chord, ARP the pings, LFO the bass, SEQ the drums) moves its sound a
# step (a walk pulled back to the piece's recipe), says the biggest change and shows the layer's sound page; held
# on, a shake (a new voice or kit, every value a big step);
# a tap is the page, as ever. (1.4.0, format 29, the variety plan: nothing nudges by itself any more: Evolve's own
# nudges gone with Evolve; Vary turns the patterns, not the sound)
listen
wait 2000
press ENV
wait 700
release ENV
wait 300
said CHORD NUDGE
expect view 31
press ARP
wait 700
release ARP
wait 300
said PINGS NUDGE
expect view 9
press LFO
wait 700
release LFO
wait 300
said BASS NUDGE
expect view 10
press SEQ
wait 700
release SEQ
wait 300
said DRUMS NUDGE
# (1.4.0: the page whose knob moved most: the Kick page, or the Hats page)
expect view >10
# held on (1.5 s): a shake, a new voice (Basic's chord: Saws, 0) and every value a big step
press ENV
wait 1800
release ENV
wait 300
said CHORD SHAKE
expect par22 >0
expect view 8
# held on, the drums: another kit
press SEQ
wait 1800
release SEQ
wait 300
said DRUMS SHAKE
expect par35 >0
# the bass held on: a shake, a new voice and a new groove (a neighbour)
press LFO
wait 1800
release LFO
wait 300
said BASS SHAKE
expect view 10
# FX, the space: a nudge, then held on a shake (a new echo time); the Dub page
press FX
wait 700
release FX
wait 300
said SPACE NUDGE
expect view 5
press FX
wait 1800
release FX
wait 300
said SPACE SHAKE
# a tap: the page (no nudge)
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
said_none NUDGE
# Vary 40: two minutes playing, nothing nudged (saved, then still saved)
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 0
spin K2 -10
wait 200
expect par5 40
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
wait 300
expect dirty 0
wait 120000
expect dirty 0
# Vary 100: two minutes, nothing nudged (Evolve 100 nudged the sound: no more; the bass held, its Vary at Hold, so
# its borrowed groove rests too): saved, then still saved
tap LFO
wait 300
spin K2 -60
wait 300
expect par136 -50
tap HOME
wait 300
spin K2 60
wait 200
expect par5 100
press GLO
wait 600
release GLO
wait 300
expect dirty 0
wait 120000
expect dirty 0
# a nudge of yours shows a card in the middle (amber), a shake's red; gone after ~1.8 s
tap HOME
wait 2500
expect card 0
press ENV
wait 700
release ENV
wait 200
expect card 1
wait 2000
expect card 0
press LFO
wait 1700
release LFO
wait 200
expect card 2
# every long press its card: EDIT held (the next chord), held on (new chords, red); GLO held (saved), held on (reset)
wait 2000
press EDIT
wait 700
release EDIT
wait 200
expect card 1
wait 2000
press EDIT
wait 1700
release EDIT
wait 200
expect card 2
wait 2000
press GLO
wait 700
release GLO
wait 200
expect card 1
wait 2000
press GLO
wait 1700
release GLO
wait 200
expect card 2
# HOME held on: a shake of everything (the chord's, the pings', the bass's voices and the kit, the noise's character);
# the page kept; HOME with SELECT turned is still the tempo
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
turn PRESET 1
turn PRESET -1
press GLO
wait 1700
release GLO
wait 300
expect par22 0
expect par35 0
press HOME
wait 1700
release HOME
wait 200
said SHAKE EVERYTHING
expect card 2
expect view 1
expect par22 !=0
expect par35 !=0
